W R1c PASS an L1 worker still cannot record a human answer to a Human Decision Gate after the rewrite -- {"ok": false, "code": "AUTHORITY_DENIED"}
W R1d PASS mutating operations fail closed (KERNEL_TAMPERED) -- KERNEL_TAMPERED
W R1e PASS doctor is UNHEALTHY and D003 names the rewritten file -- {"verdict": "UNHEALTHY", "D003": [{"id": "D003", "name": "kernel payload integrity", "ok": false, "severity": "critical", "message": "modified=[\"policies/AUTHORITY_POLICY.yaml\"] missing=[] added=[]", "remediation": "gov kernel reinstall --source <release> (kernel is immutable, INV-007)"}]}
W R1f PASS the rewritten installation is not presented as current -- UNAUTHENTICATED
W R1h PASS a reinstall against the rewritten pin is refused before anything moves, naming the pin this machine recorded -- {"code": "KERNEL_PIN_REWRITTEN", "installation_unchanged": true, "recorded": {"release_hash": "67e8071e5bca4c1887c9a148a9f94e0acd2d31161101a7efda91f005921a8f5b", "kernel_manifest_hash": "31ffbd1ccf9076af991be36b54f16c2cd1a5233d63f4482d70c5823c2eff3428", "release_version": "4.1.5", "ingress": "init", "at": "2026-09-19T00:57:20Z"}}
W R1g PASS remedy: pin restored, `gov kernel reinstall --source <signed release>` restores a trusted kernel; the L3 floor is back -- {"reinstall": true, "verified": true, "gate_create": true, "l1_decide": "AUTHORITY_DENIED"}

## R2 unprovisioned machine: consistent rewrite of a project this machine installed
W R2a PASS on the default posture the rewrite is REPORTED: kernel trust names the divergence and the presentation discloses it -- {"protected_record": {"state": "DIVERGED_NOT_ENFORCED", "basis": "the installed payload ce80feec4dbce8c8b9369cc213a81d1c8c27fc30ce70ce1229539fae1840ed42 is not the payload 67e8071e5bca4c1887c9a148a9f94e0acd2d31161101a7efda91f005921a8f5b this machine installed into this project. This machine holds no trust anchor, so its record is itself unauthenticated: the divergence is reported, not enforced (OD-P2-02 is with the owner)"}, "presented_as": "UNAUTHENTICATED", "disclosure": "release authenticity UNKNOWN: this machine holds no provisioned Signed Release Root trust anchor, so no installation on it can be authenticated. It is not current, not verified and not certified (Contract v3:150). Provision a trust anchor (`gov trust provision --anchor <administrator root>`) and ins"}
O R2b not enforced on the unprovisioned posture (OD-P2-02 is with the owner): kernel trust verified=True, task create -> True

## R3 a second provisioned machine that did not install the project (git clone)
