=================== WS08-P3-certification-and-lock-identity.py ===================
## C1/C2 provisioned machine, update gating
W C1a PASS an unsigned CERTIFIED claim does not waive the Human Decision Gate -- {"certification": "UNCERTIFIED", "human_gate_required": true, "certification_basis": {"authenticated": false, "authenticated_status": null, "release_metadata_sha256": "ee583a620e6c3d6c52522e76b8bf0bcdbe6116fd1cc5176e568b3523b573d7b4", "release_version": "4.1.6", "basis": "the signed release metadata binds no certification evidence; treated as uncertified", "unsigned_claim": "CERTIFIED", "unsigned_claim_disposition": "a request, recorded and ignored (D-0007 rule 2): an unsigned certification claim is treated as uncertified everywhere"}}
W C1b PASS `gov update --apply` stops at the gate; nothing is installed -- {"code": "HUMAN_GATE_REQUIRED", "lock_version": "4.1.5"}
W C2a PASS a certification bound by signed release metadata is authenticated against this machine's trust root -- {"certification": "CERTIFIED", "human_gate_required": false, "certification_basis": {"authenticated": true, "authenticated_status": "CERTIFIED", "release_metadata_sha256": "cd0205a28a66daebd739bc6d222d4e8c035a66cd980255419147bb32205652e6", "release_version": "4.1.6", "basis": "certification status 'CERTIFIED' is bound by release metadata signed under the `release` role of this machine's trusted root (release.json sha256 cd0205a28a66daebd739bc6d222d4e8c035a66cd980255419147bb32205652e6)", "unsigned_claim": "READY_FOR_INDEPENDENT_OS_VERIFICATION", "unsigned_claim_disposition": "a request, recorded and ignored (D-0007 rule 2): an unsigned certification claim is treated as uncertified everywhere"}}
W C2b PASS that authenticated certification — and only it — lets the update proceed without a gate -- {"ok": true, "applied": true, "code": null}

