=================== WS08-P4-rollback-and-atomicity.py ===================
## K1 provisioned rollback after a gated update
W K1a PASS precondition: the update to authentic 4.1.6 is applied through its Human Decision Gate -- {"gate": "HDG-0001", "code": null, "lock": "4.1.6"}
W K1b PASS without break-glass the floor refuses the rollback (OWNER-DECISION-0006 §9) -- SRR_BELOW_FLOOR
W K1c PASS the refused rollback leaves the installation as it found it (lock, trusted kernel, unconsumed snapshot) -- {"verified": true, "snapshots": ["4.1.6"]}
W K1d PASS `update --rollback --break-glass` restores 4.1.5, authenticated from this machine's own record of verifying it -- {"ok": true, "code": null, "lock": "4.1.5", "authenticity": "PREVIOUSLY_VERIFIED_BY_THIS_MACHINE", "kernel_verified": true}
W K1e PASS the machine is marked DEGRADED — RECOVERY ONLY and no floor moved (OWNER-DECISION-0006 §4, §8) -- {"degraded": "DEGRADED \u2014 RECOVERY ONLY", "high_water": {"version": "4.1.6", "sequence": 20}}

## K2 [K6a] shape: break-glass reinstall of an older authentic release (a version change)
W K2a PASS refused as a version change; kernel, lock, trusted state and the protected installed record are exactly as before -- {"code": "KERNEL_MISMATCH", "kernel_unchanged": true, "verified": true}
O K2b machine marking after the refused reinstall: DEGRADED — RECOVERY ONLY — the verifier enters break-glass before the pin is known to it; with IP-3 (cli/src/main.rs passes `.with_pinned_payload(framework.lock release_hash)`) the refusal precedes break-glass entry and no owner authorisation is consumed

## K3 [V1]-[V3] shape: reinstall of a newer authentic release, no break-glass
W K3a PASS refused before the swap: the installed kernel is still 4.1.5 under a 4.1.5 lock and governed work continues -- {"code": "KERNEL_MISMATCH", "kernel": "4.1.5", "lock": "4.1.5", "task_create": true}

## K4 a refused update leaves no snapshot behind
W K4a PASS the unsigned update is refused by the single verifier and leaves no snapshot -- {"code": "SRR_RELEASE_UNVERIFIED", "snapshots": []}
W K4b PASS `gov update --rollback` finds nothing to roll back and writes no false ledger entry -- {"code": "SNAPSHOT_MISSING", "ledger_events": []}

## K5 transaction abort restores the protected record with the bytes
W K5a PASS precondition: the update aborts in its post-install suite and restores the pre-update lock -- {"code": "OVERLAY_INVALID"}
W K5b PASS after the abort the restored kernel matches this machine's protected record and governed work continues -- {"verified": true, "summary": "installed kernel 4.1.4 intact: matches KERNEL_MANIFEST.json, framework.lock and this machine's protected installation record", "task_create": true}
